<rml>
<head>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="theme.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="options.rcss"/>
</head>
<body data-model="options">
    <!-- Tier 4 screen #1 (options_manager::show, standalone mode = world_options_only
         false: main-menu Options + in-game Options). The canonical tabbed FORM — this
         screen matures the form/tab-page sub-pattern the other Tier-4 giants reuse.
         Page tabs (shared theme .tabs/.tab, dynamic Vector) over a grouped two-column
         list: each row = number + name + value, with collapsible group-header rows.
         A tooltip pane (top) renders the selected entry's folded help text. The curses
         scrollbar + iStartPos windowing are dropped for native RmlUi scroll. All editing
         stays on input_context (LEFT/RIGHT/CONFIRM change values, int/float open a
         string_input popup, CONFIRM on a header collapses it); the doc is render-only and
         handles mouse selection (click only — no mouseover, so a parked mouse can't steal
         the keyboard cursor). world_options_only mode (worldgen tabs) is slice 2. -->
    <div class="panel opt-panel">
        <div class="opt-tooltip" data-rml="tooltip_rml"></div>

        <div class="tabs opt-tabs">
            <div class="item tab" data-for="t : tabs"
                 data-class-selected="t.selected"
                 data-event-click="on_tab(it_index)" data-rml="t.name_rml"></div>
        </div>

        <div id="opt-list" class="opt-list scroll-pane">
            <div class="opt-row" data-for="r : rows"
                 data-class-header="r.is_header"
                 data-class-selected="r.selected"
                 data-event-click="on_select(it_index)">
                <span class="opt-num" data-rml="r.num_rml"></span>
                <span class="opt-name" data-rml="r.name_rml"></span>
                <span class="opt-value" data-rml="r.value_rml"></span>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</body>
</rml>
